  notes: Both JCM548 and1136 explicitly add separately autoclaved1MGlucose stock.
    JCM548 says autoclave and store the non-bicarbonate stocks anaerobically underN2;
    JCM1136 adds stock aseptically and anaerobically after cooling. Glucose stereochemistry,
    anomer and starting hydrate are not stated. The stock solvent composition and
    preparation volume are unreported. Water is omitted from components; closure remains
    UNKNOWN. Gas handling is retained as a preparation instruction without asserting
    a dissolved gas component. Whole solution is distinct from D-glucose solute aliases.
    JCM1406 and1412 independently specify1M glucose stock20ml/L;1406 identifies autoclaved
    stock additions and1412 explicitly autoclaved storage underN2. Preserve each source
    preparation statement without inferring unstated storage conditions in1406. Same
    generic glucose/1M scope and unknown anomer/hydrate apply; no global glucose-solution
    alias.
notes: 'Both JCM548 and1136 explicitly add separately autoclaved1MGlucose stock. JCM548
  says autoclave and store the non-bicarbonate stocks anaerobically underN2; JCM1136
  adds stock aseptically and anaerobically after cooling. Glucose stereochemistry,
  anomer and starting hydrate are not stated. The stock solvent composition and preparation
  volume are unreported. Water is omitted from components; closure remains UNKNOWN.
  Gas handling is retained as a preparation instruction without asserting a dissolved
  gas component. Whole solution is distinct from D-glucose solute aliases. Raw source
  label retained for this occurrence only: ''1 M Glucose''. Generic wording is not
  a global resolving alias. JCM1406 and1412 independently specify1M glucose stock20ml/L;1406
  identifies autoclaved stock additions and1412 explicitly autoclaved storage underN2.
  Preserve each source preparation statement without inferring unstated storage conditions
  in1406. Same generic glucose/1M scope and unknown anomer/hydrate apply; no global
  glucose-solution alias.'
